<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 25 August, from 325 to 2012.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-council-of-nicaea" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-council-of-nicaea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">325 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,701 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The First Council of Nicaea closes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By tradition the council summoned by Constantine ended on this date. It had condemned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arianism">Arianism</a>, adopted the Nicene Creed and set rules for dating Easter, shaping Christian doctrine for centuries.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">383 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,643 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Gratian is murdered after surrendering to Magnus Maximus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gratian, emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a> since 367, was murdered at a banquet after surrendering to the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-maximus">Magnus Maximus</a>, who had been proclaimed emperor by his troops in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and crossed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-maximus">Magnus Maximus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1258">1258 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">768 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nicaea's regent George Mouzalon is murdered in a noble conspiracy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">George Mouzalon, a high official of the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodore-ii-laskaris">Theodore II Laskaris</a> and its regent, was assassinated in a conspiracy of nobles led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-viii-palaiologos">Michael VIII Palaiologos</a>, who became co-emperor in 1259 and recovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 1261.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-viii-palaiologos">Michael VIII Palaiologos</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1270">1270 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">756 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis IX dies at Tunis and Philip III becomes king</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a> died of dysentery at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eighth-crusade">Eighth Crusade</a>, and his son Philip III, who had accompanied him, succeeded him. Philip returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and was anointed king at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reims">Reims</a> in 1271.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iii-of-france">Philip III of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eighth-crusade">Eighth Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1609">1609 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">417 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Galileo demonstrates his telescope to Venice's rulers</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galileo-galilei">Galileo</a> showed the Venetian authorities his improved telescope, which made distant ships visible hours before they could be seen by eye. The Republic rewarded him with a lifetime post at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1825">1825 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">201 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Uruguay declares independence from Brazil</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A congress at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> declared the Banda Oriental independent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Empire of Brazil</a> and united with the River Plate provinces. After a war, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> became a sovereign state under the 1828 treaty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1919">1919 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">107 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First daily international scheduled air service begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Aircraft Transport and Travel began daily flights between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>'s Hounslow Heath and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, carrying passengers, mail and goods. It was the start of scheduled international commercial aviation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Paris is liberated from German occupation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French and American troops entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> and the German commander, General von Choltitz, surrendered, having ignored Hitler's order to destroy the city. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">De Gaulle</a> led a victory march the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2012">2012 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">14 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Neil Armstrong dies aged 82</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Neil Armstrong, the first person to walk on the Moon, died in Cincinnati after heart surgery. A modest engineer, he largely avoided the celebrity that followed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> 11.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 25 August <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-gottfried-herder"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-gottfried-herder.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Johann Gottfried Herder</span><span class="tp">1744–1803</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-i-of-bavaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ludwig-i-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ludwig I of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">1786–1868</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/luis-alves-de-lima-e-silva-duke-of-caxias"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/luis-alves-de-lima-e-silva-duke-of-caxias.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Luís Alves de Lima e Silva, Duke of Caxias</span><span class="tp">1803–1880</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-ii-of-bavaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ludwig-ii-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ludwig II of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">1845–1886</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 25 August <span class="n">11</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dietrich-of-haldensleben"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Dietrich of Haldensleben</span><span class="tp">d. 985</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hugh-iii-duke-of-burgundy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hugh-iii-duke-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hugh III, Duke of Burgundy</span><span class="tp">1142–1192</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-ix-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis IX of France</span><span class="tp">1214–1270</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/joan-countess-of-toulouse"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/joan-countess-of-toulouse.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joan, Countess of Toulouse</span><span class="tp">1220–1271</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/margaret-of-anjou"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/margaret-of-anjou.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Margaret of Anjou</span><span class="tp">1430–1482</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-iv-landgrave-of-hesse-kassel"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-iv-landgrave-of-hesse-kassel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William IV, Landgrave of Hesse-Kassel</span><span class="tp">1532–1592</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-morgan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-morgan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry Morgan</span><span class="tp">c. 1635–1688</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/david-hume"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/david-hume.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">David Hume</span><span class="tp">1711–1776</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/thomas-chittenden"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/thomas-chittenden.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Thomas Chittenden</span><span class="tp">1730–1797</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-watt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-watt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James Watt</span><span class="tp">1736–1819</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/michael-faraday"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/michael-faraday.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Michael Faraday</span><span class="tp">1791–1867</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
